notes.content:
We’ve added two new options to the game settings that will allow you to run the game with a more stable frame rate.

[list]
[*]Added the ability to switch the graphics API from DirectX12 to Vulkan;
[*]Added the ability to disable global illumination (Lumen/RTX);
[/list]

Patch Notes:

[list]
[*]Added icons for ladders on the map;
[*]Added a player indicator to the map;
[*]Increased the game's Hard difficulty: enemies are faster, and health no longer recovers when saving;
[/list]

Thank you for your support and feedback — it really helps us make the game better!

Changes in this patch:

[list]
[*]Fixed lighting artifacts in the hospital complex;
[*]The shotgun is now immediately equipped when picked up;
[*]Fixed various issues with the Damage Ability;
[*]Reduced flashlight brightness on low graphics settings;
[*]Removed the “Load Game” option upon death (you can now only start a new loop);
[*]Improved enemy hit detection physics;
[*]Shooting an enemy in the leg now slows him down;
[*]Increased the volume of enemy hit sounds;
[/list]

Thank you for your support and feedback — it really helps us make the game better!

Over this short time since the release of the prologue, we’ve been gathering your feedback and decided to release a small update that fixes some bugs and adds new features to the game:

[list]
[*]Added mouse sensitivity settings for both regular gameplay and aiming;
[*]The shotgun now always knocks enemies back;
[*]A headshot with a pistol now slows enemies down for 1–2 seconds;
[*]Added a heartbeat volume slider;
[*]Fixed repeating text in the ability tooltip;
[*]Removed the “Confirm” prompt in the UI for the locked locker in the Locker Room;
[/list]

Thank you so much for sharing your impressions with us! Together, we’ll make the game even better 🙂
